### Global Warming journal-entry widgets, laid out to docs/guides/gui_style_guide.md.
###
### LAYOUT. Three named roots at the foot of this file, attached by
### common/journal_entries/je_global_warming.txt:
###   widget_je_gw_overview  -> custom_widget_container_1 (above the status line)
###       te_gw_overview_panel: tier, market role, penalty scale and, while one
###       binds us, the treaty; the temperature bar with its next-threshold
###       marker and "1.61 -> 1.81 C (+0.02/yr)" headline (the reading, then
###       the reading in ten years at last year's rate); the yearly emissions
###       table; the share and cut pies. Always shown. It replaces the entry's status line, which now
###       prints only while the entry is inactive, and vanilla's goal bar near
###       the foot: the entry puts the bars-on-top marker in
###       custom_widget_container_7 (which hides the goal bar from #582 on).
###   widget_je_gw_status    -> custom_widget_container_2 (below the status line,
###                             above the vanilla button grid, which is hidden
###                             from humans)
###       te_gw_status_sections: Mitigation Policies (the eight rows, with
###       Around the World nested) and Top Emitters (the five markets emitting
###       most, named by their leaders). Open.
###   widget_je_gw_reference -> custom_widget_container_3 (below the grid)
###       te_gw_reference_sections: History (the two charts, open) and How
###       Global Warming Works (every explanation, collapsed).
### Each section is a type, so the Market panel's Climate tab
### (gui/market_panel.gui) composes the same pieces (style rule 9); the roots
### are thin wrappers that repeat the composers' [JournalEntry.IsActive] gate.
### Nothing here may read the panel's ambient Market or Country: under the tab
### it is the market the panel shows (MarketTabTest).
###
### Collapse flags say their default: *_closed sections are open until closed,
### *_open ones collapsed until opened (test_global_warming_layout.py).
###
### Every yes/no question and every action is answered by a scripted GUI in
### common/scripted_guis/global_warming_sguis.txt, which delegates to the same
### gw_possible_* / gw_effect_* helpers as the journal-entry buttons. Nothing here
### holds gameplay state; the only widget-local state is the GUI variable system
### flags that collapse the sections.
###
### OP CODES (must match the header of global_warming_sguis.txt)
###   0  Adopt   1  Repeal
### Identical for all eight policies, so they are baked into gw_adopt_button /
### gw_repeal_button and a row instance carries no op markup.
###
### DATA CONTRACT — nothing below re-derives a threshold or a balance number:
###   is it in force      -> GetScriptedGui('gw_active_<policy>_sgui').IsShown,
###                          which delegates to gw_policy_<policy>_active
###   can I adopt/repeal  -> ScriptedGui.IsValid, i.e. gw_possible_*
###   why is it greyed    -> ScriptedGui.IsValidTooltip (conditions with ticks)
###   what would it do    -> ScriptedGui.ExecuteTooltip, which renders the
###                          policy's GW_*_DESC including its
###                          [GetStaticModifier(...).GetDesc] effect list
###   severity tier       -> ScriptValue('gw_disp_tier_code') for the icon,
###                          GetCustom('gw_severity_short'/'gw_severity_text')
###                          for the word and the sentence; the code is the
###                          ladder's one definition (global_warming_values.txt)
###   bar, marker, pies   -> the gw_disp_* values in global_warming_values.txt
###   every figure        -> a ScriptValue from global_warming_values.txt, all of
###                          them O(1) reads over pulse-written snapshots
###
### MARKET LEADERSHIP IS NOT A VISIBILITY RULE. All eight rows render for every
### country, because the three market-wide policies are applied to a market
### MEMBER's journal entry by its leader. A member sees them lit and "Active",
### with "Set by our market leader" said once above them and a greyed control.
###
### The two charts reuse te_history_chart from te_history_chart.gui; the samples
### come from common/scripted_effects/te_history_global_warming_effects.txt.
###
### The icons are the painted set in gfx/interface/icons/gw_icons/ (PR #586),
### except the in-force check and Treaty-Bound, which stay vanilla marks. Each
### is a literal `texture` line below; docs/systems/global_warming_gui_icons.md
### records what each shows, and test_global_warming_layout.py
### (GwIconsTest) holds each code to its file.

types global_warming_widget_types
{
	### ======================================================================
	### BUILDING BLOCKS. The UN's (un_chamber_widget.gui), gw_-prefixed, so
	### this file depends on no other system's file loading first.
	### ======================================================================

	### A live line: the section's own text type (style rule 7).
	type gw_text = textbox {
		autoresize = yes
		multiline = yes
		minimumsize = { 480 -1 }
		maximumsize = { 480 -1 }
		align = left|nobaseline
		using = fontsize_large
	}

	### A section's body, under its header.
	type gw_panel = flowcontainer {
		direction = vertical
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		parentanchor = hcenter
		margin = { 20 8 }
		spacing = 4

		background = {
			using = entry_bg_fancy_dark
			alpha = 0.5
		}
	}

	### Collapsible section header. The flag lives in the GUI variable system
	### only — presentation state, never written to the save.
	type gw_section_header = section_header_button {
		blockoverride "layout" {
			parentanchor = hcenter
			size = { 520 38 }
		}
	}

	### A heading inside a section's panel, over one group of its lines, with a
	### faint rule under it (gui_modding_guide.md gotcha #26).
	type gw_subheader = flowcontainer {
		direction = vertical
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		spacing = 1
		block "subheader_margin" {
			margin_top = 6
		}

		textbox = {
			autoresize = yes
			multiline = yes
			maximumsize = { 480 -1 }
			align = left|nobaseline
			using = fontsize_large
			default_format = "#title"
			block "subheader_text" {}
		}
		divider_clean = {
			blockoverride "size" {
				size = { 480 2 }
			}
		}
	}

	### Explanatory text under a heading, for How Global Warming Works only.
	### Static keys: the datacontext is the journal entry.
	type gw_note = textbox {
		autoresize = yes
		multiline = yes
		minimumsize = { 480 -1 }
		maximumsize = { 480 -1 }
		align = left|nobaseline
		using = fontsize_medium
		default_format = "#lore"
	}

	### An expandable section nested inside another section's panel: narrower,
	### lower and smaller than gw_section_header, set in by its holder.
	type gw_subsection_header = section_header_button {
		blockoverride "layout" {
			size = { 440 30 }
		}
		blockoverride "fontsize" {
			using = fontsize_medium
		}
		blockoverride "arrow_size" {
			size = { 20 20 }
		}
		blockoverride "left_textbox_margin_left" {
			margin_left = 32
		}
	}

	### A table row: a label on the left and its value on the right (style
	### rule 5; un_chamber_value_row's shape). 340 + 120: the value column is
	### wide enough for "136 nations" (play-test round 3's width budget).
	type gw_value_row = flowcontainer {
		direction = horizontal
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		margin = { 4 1 }

		textbox = {
			autoresize = yes
			minimumsize = { 340 -1 }
			maximumsize = { 340 -1 }
			align = left|nobaseline
			using = fontsize_medium
			elide = right
			block "row_label" {}
		}
		textbox = {
			autoresize = yes
			minimumsize = { 120 -1 }
			maximumsize = { 120 -1 }
			align = right|nobaseline
			using = fontsize_medium
			default_format = "#v"
			block "row_value" {}
		}
	}

	### The Adopt control. Op 0 is baked in, so a row instance only supplies the
	### datacontext naming its policy's handler. No `visible` here: the enclosing
	### widget in gw_policy_row decides which of the pair is rendered (two
	### `visible` properties on one widget is a bug, not a conjunction).
	###
	### Both read `Country`, the datacontext te_gw_sec_policies sets on its root
	### (block "gw_market_country": the entry's country in the journal, the
	### shown market's leader in the Market panel's Climate tab on another
	### market). They are greyed unless that country is the local player
	### (Country.IsLocalPlayer, vanilla's test in military_formation_panel.gui,
	### right_click_menu.gui and vanilla loc): always true in the journal, false
	### on another market, where the tooltip says whose policies these are. The
	### handlers' effects also require is_player (global_warming_sguis.txt).
	###
	### `button` + `using = default_button_action` is the in-game text-button
	### idiom (vanilla scripted_journal_entry_button); the button_standard_*
	### family is frontend-only and never instantiated in game.
	type gw_adopt_button = button {
		using = default_button_action
		size = { 104 30 }
		parentanchor = vcenter
		text = "gw_btn_adopt"
		enabled = "[And( Country.IsLocalPlayer, ScriptedGui.IsValid( GuiScope.SetRoot( Country.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)0' ) ).End ) )]"
		onclick = "[ScriptedGui.Execute( GuiScope.SetRoot( Country.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)0' ) ).End )]"
		tooltip = "[SelectLocalization( Country.IsLocalPlayer, Concatenate( ScriptedGui.IsValidTooltip( GuiScope.SetRoot( Country.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)0' ) ).End ), Concatenate( Localize( 'te_tt_break' ), ScriptedGui.ExecuteTooltip( GuiScope.SetRoot( Country.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)0' ) ).End ) ) ), 'gw_btn_not_ours_tt' )]"
	}

	### The Repeal control, op 1. Stays visible and greyed when a treaty or
	### market membership blocks rollback, so the reason is readable.
	type gw_repeal_button = button {
		using = default_button_action
		size = { 104 30 }
		parentanchor = vcenter
		text = "gw_btn_repeal"
		enabled = "[And( Country.IsLocalPlayer, ScriptedGui.IsValid( GuiScope.SetRoot( Country.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)1' ) ).End ) )]"
		onclick = "[ScriptedGui.Execute( GuiScope.SetRoot( Country.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)1' ) ).End )]"
		tooltip = "[SelectLocalization( Country.IsLocalPlayer, Concatenate( ScriptedGui.IsValidTooltip( GuiScope.SetRoot( Country.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)1' ) ).End ), Concatenate( Localize( 'te_tt_break' ), ScriptedGui.ExecuteTooltip( GuiScope.SetRoot( Country.MakeScope ).AddScope( 'op', MakeScopeValue( '(CFixedPoint)1' ) ).End ) ) ), 'gw_btn_not_ours_tt' )]"
	}

	### One policy: its icon, lit while in force and dimmed while not (style
	### rule 4; hover: in force or not), its name (hover: what it does), a
	### green check while in force, and exactly one of the Adopt / Repeal
	### controls beside it. Fixed-width cells, 26 + 276 + 24 + 110 and the
	### gaps and margins = 466 px, so nothing can widen the row. The check
	### replaced the "Active"/"Inactive" word in play-test round 3, which
	### freed the width the names needed: the longest, "Reforestation
	### Subsidies", is 23 characters, about 253 units in the large font.
	###
	### The row's datacontext is the policy's gw_active_<policy>_sgui, so
	### `ScriptedGui.IsShown` below is "is this policy in force for us?". The
	### buttons carry their own datacontext (the action handler) inside the
	### adopt_action / repeal_action blocks.
	type gw_policy_row = flowcontainer {
		direction = horizontal
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		spacing = 6
		margin = { 6 3 }
		parentanchor = hcenter

		background = {
			using = entry_bg_fancy_dark
			alpha = 0.35
		}

		widget = {
			size = { 26 26 }
			parentanchor = vcenter
			tooltip = "[SelectLocalization( ScriptedGui.IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( Country.MakeScope ).End ), 'gw_policy_status_active', 'gw_policy_status_inactive' )]"

			icon = {
				size = { 26 26 }
				parentanchor = center
				visible = "[ScriptedGui.IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( Country.MakeScope ).End )]"
				block "row_icon" {}
			}
			icon = {
				size = { 26 26 }
				parentanchor = center
				alpha = 0.25
				visible = "[Not( ScriptedGui.IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( Country.MakeScope ).End ) )]"
				block "row_icon" {}
			}
		}

		### The name. The instance's block sets the text and the tooltip, the
		### policy's GW_*_DESC with its effect list: the Repeal control's
		### tooltip shows only what repealing does, so this is where a policy in
		### force says what it is doing.
		widget = {
			size = { 276 26 }
			parentanchor = vcenter

			textbox = {
				parentanchor = left|vcenter
				autoresize = yes
				max_width = 276
				elide = right
				align = nobaseline
				using = fontsize_large
				default_format = "#tooltippable"
				block "row_label" {}
			}
		}

		### A green check while in force; nothing while not (the dimmed icon
		### beside the name already says so).
		widget = {
			size = { 24 26 }
			parentanchor = vcenter

			icon = {
				size = { 20 20 }
				parentanchor = center
				visible = "[ScriptedGui.IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( Country.MakeScope ).End )]"
				texture = "gfx/interface/icons/generic_icons/green_checkmark.dds"
				tooltip = "gw_policy_status_active"
			}
		}

		### Exactly one control. Adopt while the policy is not in force, Repeal
		### while it is — the same question that drives the icon and the status
		### cell, asked of the same scripted GUI.
		widget = {
			size = { 110 30 }
			parentanchor = vcenter

			widget = {
				size = { 100% 100% }
				visible = "[Not( ScriptedGui.IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( Country.MakeScope ).End ) )]"
				block "adopt_action" {}
			}

			widget = {
				size = { 100% 100% }
				visible = "[ScriptedGui.IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( Country.MakeScope ).End )]"
				block "repeal_action" {}
			}
		}
	}

	### ======================================================================
	### OVERVIEW. Always shown: the state a returning player checks.
	### ======================================================================

	### A cell of the overview's first row: an icon, its word small beneath.
	### Fixed width, so the row cannot push the panel wider (te_un_ov_icon_label).
	type te_gw_ov_icon_label = widget {
		size = { 110 58 }

		icon = {
			size = { 36 36 }
			parentanchor = top|hcenter
			block "icon_texture" {}
		}
		textbox = {
			parentanchor = bottom|hcenter
			autoresize = yes
			max_width = 108
			elide = right
			align = hcenter|nobaseline
			using = fontsize_small
			default_format = "#tooltippable"
			block "label" {}
		}
	}

	### A 0..1 share as a pie over a background disc, inside vanilla's
	### decorated round frame, its label beneath (te_un_ov_pie; the recipe is
	### gui_modding_guide.md "Pie charts of script-held data"). The instance
	### names the fill texture: frame 1 transparent, frame 2 the colour. 176
	### wide, so "Emissions Cut 100%" fits beneath (play-test round 3).
	type te_gw_ov_pie = widget {
		size = { 176 108 }

		icon = {
			size = { 86 86 }
			parentanchor = top|hcenter
			texture = "gfx/interface/backgrounds/round_frame_dec.dds"
		}
		widget = {
			size = { 62 62 }
			parentanchor = top|hcenter
			position = { 0 12 }

			progresspie = {
				size = { 100% 100% }
				min = 0
				max = 1
				value = 1
				texture = "gfx/interface/icons/un_icons/pie_rest.dds"
				framesize = { 128 128 }
				frame = 2
			}
			progresspie = {
				size = { 100% 100% }
				min = 0
				max = 1
				block "pie_value" {}
				block "pie_fill" {
					texture = "gfx/interface/icons/un_icons/pie_members.dds"
				}
				framesize = { 128 128 }
				frame = 2
			}
		}
		textbox = {
			parentanchor = bottom|hcenter
			autoresize = yes
			max_width = 176
			elide = right
			align = hcenter|nobaseline
			using = fontsize_medium
			default_format = "#tooltippable"
			block "label" {}
		}
	}

	### The overview. Its market cells (row 1's role and treaty cells; the
	### market's emissions and capture rows; the two pies) read `Country`, set
	### by block "gw_market_country" on the four widgets that hold them. The
	### block's default is the entry's own country, so the journal and the
	### Market panel's Climate tab on the player's own market read as before;
	### the tab on another market overrides it with that market's leader
	### (MarketPanel.GetMarket.GetOwner), so those cells show the market the
	### panel shows. Everything else, row 1's tier and penalty included, reads
	### JournalEntry, which stays the player's entry: the temperature and the
	### world's figures stay the player's view (market_panel.gui). Not the
	### leader's journal entry: in game Country.GetJournalEntry either failed
	### at load or silently kept the player's entry (gui_modding_guide.md
	### gotcha #35). Labels that say "our" pick their
	### wording on Country.IsLocalPlayer, as the policy controls do.
	type te_gw_overview_panel = flowcontainer {
		direction = vertical
		parentanchor = hcenter
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		visible = "[JournalEntry.IsActive]"

		gw_panel = {
			### One 480 px column, so the panel is as wide as the sections below
			### (520 with its margins) from the first layout on; the UN overview
			### pins its rows the same way. Without it the block sat ~70 px in
			### from the column and ran off the panel's right edge (play-test
			### round 1, 2026-09-29): by the numbers, centred at row 1's width
			### (3 x 110 + gaps + margins = 382, (520 - 382) / 2 = 69) before the
			### temperature headline's text widened row 2.
			flowcontainer = {
				direction = vertical
				spacing = 10
				ignoreinvisible = yes
				minimumsize = { 480 -1 }

				### Row 1: tier · market role · penalty scale · treaty (while bound)
				flowcontainer = {
					direction = horizontal
					spacing = 6
					ignoreinvisible = yes
					parentanchor = hcenter
					block "gw_market_country" {
						datacontext = "[JournalEntry.GetCountry]"
					}

					### The tier, one icon per gw_disp_tier_code; the word is
					### gw_severity_short and the tooltip the tier's sentence.
					flowcontainer = {
						ignoreinvisible = yes
						tooltip = "gw_ov_tier_tt"

						te_gw_ov_icon_label = {
							visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('gw_disp_tier_code'), '(CFixedPoint)0' )]"
							blockoverride "icon_texture" {
								texture = "gfx/interface/icons/gw_icons/tier_negligible.dds"
							}
							blockoverride "label" {
								text = "gw_cond_tier_value"
							}
						}
						te_gw_ov_icon_label = {
							visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('gw_disp_tier_code'), '(CFixedPoint)1' )]"
							blockoverride "icon_texture" {
								texture = "gfx/interface/icons/gw_icons/tier_slight.dds"
							}
							blockoverride "label" {
								text = "gw_cond_tier_value"
							}
						}
						te_gw_ov_icon_label = {
							visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('gw_disp_tier_code'), '(CFixedPoint)2' )]"
							blockoverride "icon_texture" {
								texture = "gfx/interface/icons/gw_icons/tier_moderate.dds"
							}
							blockoverride "label" {
								text = "gw_cond_tier_value"
							}
						}
						te_gw_ov_icon_label = {
							visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('gw_disp_tier_code'), '(CFixedPoint)3' )]"
							blockoverride "icon_texture" {
								texture = "gfx/interface/icons/gw_icons/tier_significant.dds"
							}
							blockoverride "label" {
								text = "gw_cond_tier_value"
							}
						}
						te_gw_ov_icon_label = {
							visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('gw_disp_tier_code'), '(CFixedPoint)4' )]"
							blockoverride "icon_texture" {
								texture = "gfx/interface/icons/gw_icons/tier_severe.dds"
							}
							blockoverride "label" {
								text = "gw_cond_tier_value"
							}
						}
						te_gw_ov_icon_label = {
							visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('gw_disp_tier_code'), '(CFixedPoint)5' )]"
							blockoverride "icon_texture" {
								texture = "gfx/interface/icons/gw_icons/tier_catastrophic.dds"
							}
							blockoverride "label" {
								text = "gw_cond_tier_value"
							}
						}
						te_gw_ov_icon_label = {
							visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('gw_disp_tier_code'), '(CFixedPoint)6' )]"
							blockoverride "icon_texture" {
								texture = "gfx/interface/icons/gw_icons/tier_apocalyptic.dds"
							}
							blockoverride "label" {
								text = "gw_cond_tier_value"
							}
						}
					}

					### Market leader or member: who sets the market-wide policies.
					flowcontainer = {
						ignoreinvisible = yes
						tooltip = "gw_cond_role_tt"

						te_gw_ov_icon_label = {
							visible = "[GetScriptedGui('gw_is_market_leader_sgui').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( Country.MakeScope ).End )]"
							blockoverride "icon_texture" {
								texture = "gfx/interface/icons/gw_icons/role_leader.dds"
							}
							blockoverride "label" {
								text = "gw_cond_role_value"
							}
						}
						te_gw_ov_icon_label = {
							visible = "[Not( GetScriptedGui('gw_is_market_leader_sgui').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( Country.MakeScope ).End ) )]"
							blockoverride "icon_texture" {
								texture = "gfx/interface/icons/gw_icons/role_member.dds"
							}
							blockoverride "label" {
								text = "gw_cond_role_value"
							}
						}
					}

					### The Climate Warming modifier's scale; hover for its effects.
					te_gw_ov_icon_label = {
						tooltip = "gw_cond_penalty_tt"
						blockoverride "icon_texture" {
							texture = "gfx/interface/icons/gw_icons/penalty.dds"
						}
						blockoverride "label" {
							text = "gw_ov_penalty_label"
						}
					}

					### Only while an Enforce Emissions Reduction treaty binds us.
					te_gw_ov_icon_label = {
						visible = "[GetScriptedGui('gw_treaty_bound_sgui').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( Country.MakeScope ).End )]"
						tooltip = "gw_ov_treaty_tt"
						blockoverride "icon_texture" {
							texture = "gfx/interface/icons/diplomatic_treaties_articles_icons/enforce_emissions_reduction.dds"
						}
						blockoverride "label" {
							text = "gw_ov_treaty_label"
						}
					}
				}

				### Row 2: the temperature on the journal entry's 0-4 C scale, and the
				### headline: the reading, then the reading in
				### gw_disp_projection_years (10) at last year's rate. Three fixed
				### cells, 106 + 160 + 198 and two 8 px gaps = 480: the label and the
				### headline elide inside their cells rather than widen the row.
				###
				### THE BAR (play-test round 3, 2026-09-30; the Nuclear taboo bar
				### follows the same spec). Five layers in one fixed 160 x 18 cell,
				### bottom to top. The solid fill runs to the lower of reading and
				### projection; a translucent segment runs from there to the higher.
				### THE SEGMENT'S COLOUR SAYS WHETHER THE CHANGE IS GOOD OR BAD FOR
				### THE PLAYER, not its direction (the owner's convention for every
				### projection bar: red bad, green good, the bar's own fill, pale, for
				### a neutral change). Where it sits already shows the direction:
				### past the solid fill when rising, the bar's tail when falling.
				###   1. default_progressbar_horizontal at value 0: the bar's own
				###      background and frame, no fill.
				###   2. Rising (gw_disp_temp_trend 1), i.e. warming, which is BAD:
				###      bad_progressbar_horizontal's red fill at 40% opacity (a
				###      wrapper widget, alpha = 0.4) up to the projection.
				###   3. Falling (gw_disp_temp_trend -1), i.e. cooling, which is GOOD:
				###      green_progressbar_horizontal's green fill at 50% opacity up
				###      to today's reading, the tail the temperature is set to lose.
				###   4. default_progressbar_horizontal's own fill, background and
				###      frame blanked (the UN tally's stacking), up to the lower of
				###      the two: solid.
				###   5. The next tier's threshold as a thin 3 px cream line (a
				###      progressbar marker drawn with white.dds tinted by `color`),
				###      with its own hover. None past the last threshold (tier 6).
				### No eye marker. With no rate yet (before the first January) the
				### projection equals the reading and layers 2-3 draw nothing.
				flowcontainer = {
					direction = horizontal
					spacing = 8
					tooltip = "gw_ov_temp_tt"

					widget = {
						size = { 106 24 }
						parentanchor = vcenter

						textbox = {
							parentanchor = left|vcenter
							autoresize = yes
							max_width = 106
							elide = right
							align = left|nobaseline
							text = "gw_ov_temp_label"
						}
					}
					widget = {
						size = { 160 18 }
						parentanchor = vcenter

						# 1. Background and frame.
						default_progressbar_horizontal = {
							size = { 100% 100% }
							blockoverride "values" {
								value = 0
								min = 0
								max = 1
							}
						}
						# 2. Rising, i.e. warming (bad): red, from the reading to the projection.
						widget = {
							size = { 100% 100% }
							alpha = 0.4
							visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('gw_disp_temp_trend'), '(CFixedPoint)1' )]"

							bad_progressbar_horizontal = {
								size = { 100% 100% }
								blockoverride "background" {}
								blockoverride "frame" {}
								blockoverride "values" {
									value = "[FixedPointToFloat( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('gw_disp_bar_high_frac') )]"
									min = 0
									max = 1
								}
							}
						}
						# 3. Falling, i.e. cooling (good): green, from the projection up to the reading.
						widget = {
							size = { 100% 100% }
							alpha = 0.5
							visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('gw_disp_temp_trend'), '(CFixedPoint)-1' )]"

							green_progressbar_horizontal = {
								size = { 100% 100% }
								blockoverride "background" {}
								blockoverride "frame" {}
								blockoverride "values" {
									value = "[FixedPointToFloat( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('gw_disp_bar_high_frac') )]"
									min = 0
									max = 1
								}
							}
						}
						# 4. Solid: the lower of reading and projection.
						default_progressbar_horizontal = {
							size = { 100% 100% }
							blockoverride "background" {}
							blockoverride "frame" {}
							blockoverride "values" {
								value = "[FixedPointToFloat( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('gw_disp_bar_low_frac') )]"
								min = 0
								max = 1
							}
						}
						# 5. The next tier's threshold: a thin line with its own hover.
						progressbar = {
							visible = "[Not( EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('gw_disp_tier_code'), '(CFixedPoint)6' ) )]"
							noprogresstexture = "gfx/interface/icons/generic_icons/transparent.dds"
							progresstexture = "gfx/interface/icons/generic_icons/transparent.dds"
							size = { 100% 100% }
							skip_initial_animation = yes
							direction = horizontal
							value = "[FixedPointToFloat( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('gw_disp_next_frac') )]"
							min = 0
							max = 1
							marker = {
								icon = {
									size = { 3 24 }
									parentanchor = vcenter
									widgetanchor = center
									texture = "gfx/interface/backgrounds/white.dds"
									color = { 0.96 0.90 0.72 0.95 }
									tooltip = "gw_ov_tick_tt"
								}
							}
						}
					}
					widget = {
						size = { 198 24 }
						parentanchor = vcenter

						textbox = {
							parentanchor = left|vcenter
							autoresize = yes
							max_width = 198
							elide = right
							align = left|nobaseline
							text = "gw_ov_temp_value"
						}
					}
				}

				### Row 3: the yearly emissions figures, as a table of fixed cells
				### (gw_value_row, 340 + 120) in the 480 column, beside the headline
				### whose rate they explain and above the pies they add up to. Until
				### the first January's figures exist (a new game, or a save upgraded
				### mid-year), one line saying when they arrive. It was a section of
				### its own until play-test round 3 (the owner, 2026-09-29).
				gw_text = {
					visible = "[Not( GetScriptedGui('gw_has_yearly_figures_sgui').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).End ) )]"
					align = hcenter|nobaseline
					text = "gw_emis_pending"
				}

				flowcontainer = {
					direction = vertical
					ignoreinvisible = yes
					minimumsize = { 480 -1 }
					visible = "[GetScriptedGui('gw_has_yearly_figures_sgui').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope ).End )]"

					gw_value_row = {
						block "gw_market_country" {
							datacontext = "[JournalEntry.GetCountry]"
						}
						tooltip = "gw_cond_emis_tt"
						blockoverride "row_label" {
							text = "gw_emis_market_label"
							default_format = "#tooltippable"
						}
						blockoverride "row_value" {
							text = "gw_emis_market_value"
						}
					}
					gw_value_row = {
						block "gw_market_country" {
							datacontext = "[JournalEntry.GetCountry]"
						}
						tooltip = "gw_emis_capture_tt"
						blockoverride "row_label" {
							text = "gw_emis_capture_label"
							default_format = "#tooltippable"
						}
						blockoverride "row_value" {
							text = "gw_emis_capture_value"
						}
					}
					gw_value_row = {
						tooltip = "gw_emis_world_tt"
						blockoverride "row_label" {
							text = "gw_emis_world_label"
							default_format = "#tooltippable"
						}
						blockoverride "row_value" {
							text = "gw_emis_world_value"
						}
					}
					gw_value_row = {
						tooltip = "gw_cond_trend_tt"
						blockoverride "row_label" {
							text = "gw_emis_warming_label"
							default_format = "#tooltippable"
						}
						blockoverride "row_value" {
							text = "gw_cond_trend_value"
						}
					}
				}

				### Row 4: our market's share of the world's emissions, and how far
				### its emissions are cut.
				flowcontainer = {
					direction = horizontal
					parentanchor = hcenter
					block "gw_market_country" {
						datacontext = "[JournalEntry.GetCountry]"
					}

					te_gw_ov_pie = {
						tooltip = "gw_cond_share_tt"
						blockoverride "pie_value" {
							value = "[FixedPointToFloat( Country.MakeScope.ScriptValue('gw_disp_share_frac') )]"
						}
						blockoverride "pie_fill" {
							texture = "gfx/interface/icons/gw_icons/pie_share.dds"
						}
						blockoverride "label" {
							text = "gw_ov_pie_share"
						}
					}
					te_gw_ov_pie = {
						tooltip = "gw_ov_pie_cut_tt"
						blockoverride "pie_value" {
							value = "[FixedPointToFloat( Country.MakeScope.ScriptValue('gw_disp_cut_frac') )]"
						}
						blockoverride "pie_fill" {
							texture = "gfx/interface/icons/gw_icons/pie_cut.dds"
						}
						blockoverride "label" {
							text = "gw_ov_pie_cut"
						}
					}
				}
			}
		}
	}

	### ======================================================================
	### SECTIONS. Each is composed, in order, by te_gw_status_sections or
	### te_gw_reference_sections below.
	### ======================================================================

	### Mitigation Policies: the eight rows, market-wide first. What greys every
	### Adopt or every Repeal is said once, above the rows (style rule 6), and
	### only while it holds. How many nations run each policy is a nested table
	### at the foot, open by default. Everything here reads `Country`, which
	### block "gw_market_country" sets on the root: the entry's country by
	### default, the shown market's leader in the Market panel's Climate tab on
	### another market (read-only there: gw_adopt_button).
	type te_gw_sec_policies = flowcontainer {
		direction = vertical
		parentanchor = hcenter
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		spacing = 4
		block "gw_market_country" {
			datacontext = "[JournalEntry.GetCountry]"
		}

		gw_section_header = {
			blockoverride "left_text" {
				text = "gw_sect_policies"
			}
			blockoverride "onclick" {
				onclick = "[GetVariableSystem.Toggle('gw_policies_closed')]"
			}
			blockoverride "onclick_showmore" {
				visible = "[GetVariableSystem.Exists('gw_policies_closed')]"
			}
			blockoverride "onclick_showless" {
				visible = "[Not(GetVariableSystem.Exists('gw_policies_closed'))]"
			}
		}

		gw_panel = {
			visible = "[Not(GetVariableSystem.Exists('gw_policies_closed'))]"

			# Below 0.5 C every Adopt is greyed for the same reason.
			gw_text = {
				visible = "[GetScriptedGui('gw_policies_waiting_sgui').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( Country.MakeScope ).End )]"
				align = hcenter|nobaseline
				text = "gw_pol_waiting"
			}
			# Under the treaty every Repeal but Climate Adaptation's is greyed.
			gw_text = {
				visible = "[GetScriptedGui('gw_treaty_bound_sgui').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( Country.MakeScope ).End )]"
				align = hcenter|nobaseline
				text = "gw_pol_treaty"
			}

			### ---- Market-wide (the leader sets them for the whole market) ----
			gw_subheader = {
				blockoverride "subheader_margin" {}
				blockoverride "subheader_text" {
					text = "gw_pol_sub_market"
				}
			}
			# A member's three market-wide controls are all greyed by the same
			# rule; say it once.
			gw_text = {
				visible = "[Not( GetScriptedGui('gw_is_market_leader_sgui').IsShown( GuiScope.SetRoot( Country.MakeScope ).End ) )]"
				text = "gw_pol_set_by_leader"
			}

			gw_policy_row = {
				datacontext = "[GetScriptedGui('gw_active_carbon_tax_sgui')]"
				blockoverride "row_icon" {
					texture = "gfx/interface/icons/gw_icons/policy_carbon_tax.dds"
				}
				blockoverride "row_label" {
					text = "GW_CARBON_TAX_ROW"
					tooltip = "GW_CARBON_TAX_DESC"
				}
				blockoverride "adopt_action" {
					gw_adopt_button = {
						datacontext = "[GetScriptedGui('gw_policy_carbon_tax_sgui')]"
					}
				}
				blockoverride "repeal_action" {
					gw_repeal_button = {
						datacontext = "[GetScriptedGui('gw_policy_carbon_tax_sgui')]"
					}
				}
			}

			gw_policy_row = {
				datacontext = "[GetScriptedGui('gw_active_renewable_investment_sgui')]"
				blockoverride "row_icon" {
					texture = "gfx/interface/icons/gw_icons/policy_renewable_investment.dds"
				}
				blockoverride "row_label" {
					text = "GW_RENEWABLE_INVESTMENT_ROW"
					tooltip = "GW_RENEWABLE_INVESTMENT_DESC"
				}
				blockoverride "adopt_action" {
					gw_adopt_button = {
						datacontext = "[GetScriptedGui('gw_policy_renewable_investment_sgui')]"
					}
				}
				blockoverride "repeal_action" {
					gw_repeal_button = {
						datacontext = "[GetScriptedGui('gw_policy_renewable_investment_sgui')]"
					}
				}
			}

			gw_policy_row = {
				datacontext = "[GetScriptedGui('gw_active_emission_standards_sgui')]"
				blockoverride "row_icon" {
					texture = "gfx/interface/icons/gw_icons/policy_emission_standards.dds"
				}
				blockoverride "row_label" {
					text = "GW_EMISSION_STANDARDS_ROW"
					tooltip = "GW_EMISSION_STANDARDS_DESC"
				}
				blockoverride "adopt_action" {
					gw_adopt_button = {
						datacontext = "[GetScriptedGui('gw_policy_emission_standards_sgui')]"
					}
				}
				blockoverride "repeal_action" {
					gw_repeal_button = {
						datacontext = "[GetScriptedGui('gw_policy_emission_standards_sgui')]"
					}
				}
			}

			### ---- National (every country sets its own) ----
			gw_subheader = {
				blockoverride "subheader_text" {
					text = "gw_pol_sub_national"
				}
			}

			gw_policy_row = {
				datacontext = "[GetScriptedGui('gw_active_climate_adaptation_sgui')]"
				blockoverride "row_icon" {
					texture = "gfx/interface/icons/gw_icons/policy_climate_adaptation.dds"
				}
				blockoverride "row_label" {
					text = "GW_CLIMATE_ADAPTATION_ROW"
					tooltip = "GW_CLIMATE_ADAPTATION_DESC"
				}
				blockoverride "adopt_action" {
					gw_adopt_button = {
						datacontext = "[GetScriptedGui('gw_policy_climate_adaptation_sgui')]"
					}
				}
				blockoverride "repeal_action" {
					gw_repeal_button = {
						datacontext = "[GetScriptedGui('gw_policy_climate_adaptation_sgui')]"
					}
				}
			}

			gw_policy_row = {
				datacontext = "[GetScriptedGui('gw_active_reforestation_sgui')]"
				blockoverride "row_icon" {
					texture = "gfx/interface/icons/gw_icons/policy_reforestation.dds"
				}
				blockoverride "row_label" {
					text = "GW_REFORESTATION_ROW"
					tooltip = "GW_REFORESTATION_DESC"
				}
				blockoverride "adopt_action" {
					gw_adopt_button = {
						datacontext = "[GetScriptedGui('gw_policy_reforestation_sgui')]"
					}
				}
				blockoverride "repeal_action" {
					gw_repeal_button = {
						datacontext = "[GetScriptedGui('gw_policy_reforestation_sgui')]"
					}
				}
			}

			gw_policy_row = {
				datacontext = "[GetScriptedGui('gw_active_public_transit_sgui')]"
				blockoverride "row_icon" {
					texture = "gfx/interface/icons/gw_icons/policy_public_transit.dds"
				}
				blockoverride "row_label" {
					text = "GW_PUBLIC_TRANSIT_ROW"
					tooltip = "GW_PUBLIC_TRANSIT_DESC"
				}
				blockoverride "adopt_action" {
					gw_adopt_button = {
						datacontext = "[GetScriptedGui('gw_policy_public_transit_sgui')]"
					}
				}
				blockoverride "repeal_action" {
					gw_repeal_button = {
						datacontext = "[GetScriptedGui('gw_policy_public_transit_sgui')]"
					}
				}
			}

			gw_policy_row = {
				datacontext = "[GetScriptedGui('gw_active_fossil_fuel_divestment_sgui')]"
				blockoverride "row_icon" {
					texture = "gfx/interface/icons/gw_icons/policy_fossil_fuel_divestment.dds"
				}
				blockoverride "row_label" {
					text = "GW_FOSSIL_FUEL_DIVESTMENT_ROW"
					tooltip = "GW_FOSSIL_FUEL_DIVESTMENT_DESC"
				}
				blockoverride "adopt_action" {
					gw_adopt_button = {
						datacontext = "[GetScriptedGui('gw_policy_fossil_fuel_divestment_sgui')]"
					}
				}
				blockoverride "repeal_action" {
					gw_repeal_button = {
						datacontext = "[GetScriptedGui('gw_policy_fossil_fuel_divestment_sgui')]"
					}
				}
			}

			gw_policy_row = {
				datacontext = "[GetScriptedGui('gw_active_green_building_codes_sgui')]"
				blockoverride "row_icon" {
					texture = "gfx/interface/icons/gw_icons/policy_green_building_codes.dds"
				}
				blockoverride "row_label" {
					text = "GW_GREEN_BUILDING_CODES_ROW"
					tooltip = "GW_GREEN_BUILDING_CODES_DESC"
				}
				blockoverride "adopt_action" {
					gw_adopt_button = {
						datacontext = "[GetScriptedGui('gw_policy_green_building_codes_sgui')]"
					}
				}
				blockoverride "repeal_action" {
					gw_repeal_button = {
						datacontext = "[GetScriptedGui('gw_policy_green_building_codes_sgui')]"
					}
				}
			}

			### ---- Around the World: how many nations run each policy. A live
			### table, so open by default (the owner, 2026-09-29: live lists stay
			### open, lists of past items collapse); nested, so it can be closed
			### on its own.
			flowcontainer = {
				direction = vertical
				ignoreinvisible = yes
				margin_left = 20
				margin_top = 6

				gw_subsection_header = {
					blockoverride "left_text" {
						text = "gw_sect_world"
					}
					blockoverride "onclick" {
						onclick = "[GetVariableSystem.Toggle('gw_world_closed')]"
					}
					blockoverride "onclick_showmore" {
						visible = "[GetVariableSystem.Exists('gw_world_closed')]"
					}
					blockoverride "onclick_showless" {
						visible = "[Not(GetVariableSystem.Exists('gw_world_closed'))]"
					}
				}
			}
			flowcontainer = {
				direction = vertical
				ignoreinvisible = yes
				visible = "[Not(GetVariableSystem.Exists('gw_world_closed'))]"

				gw_value_row = {
					blockoverride "row_label" {
						text = "GW_CARBON_TAX_ROW"
					}
					blockoverride "row_value" {
						text = "gw_world_n_carbon_tax"
					}
				}
				gw_value_row = {
					blockoverride "row_label" {
						text = "GW_RENEWABLE_INVESTMENT_ROW"
					}
					blockoverride "row_value" {
						text = "gw_world_n_renewable_investment"
					}
				}
				gw_value_row = {
					blockoverride "row_label" {
						text = "GW_EMISSION_STANDARDS_ROW"
					}
					blockoverride "row_value" {
						text = "gw_world_n_emission_standards"
					}
				}
				gw_value_row = {
					blockoverride "row_label" {
						text = "GW_CLIMATE_ADAPTATION_ROW"
					}
					blockoverride "row_value" {
						text = "gw_world_n_climate_adaptation"
					}
				}
				gw_value_row = {
					blockoverride "row_label" {
						text = "GW_REFORESTATION_ROW"
					}
					blockoverride "row_value" {
						text = "gw_world_n_reforestation"
					}
				}
				gw_value_row = {
					blockoverride "row_label" {
						text = "GW_PUBLIC_TRANSIT_ROW"
					}
					blockoverride "row_value" {
						text = "gw_world_n_public_transit"
					}
				}
				gw_value_row = {
					blockoverride "row_label" {
						text = "GW_FOSSIL_FUEL_DIVESTMENT_ROW"
					}
					blockoverride "row_value" {
						text = "gw_world_n_fossil_fuel_divestment"
					}
				}
				gw_value_row = {
					blockoverride "row_label" {
						text = "GW_GREEN_BUILDING_CODES_ROW"
					}
					blockoverride "row_value" {
						text = "gw_world_n_green_building_codes"
					}
				}
			}
		}
	}

	### ======================================================================
	### TOP EMITTERS (the owner, 2026-09-30: "show the top emitters, so the
	### player knows who to target for climate agreements").
	### ======================================================================

	### The headings over the rows' second line, said once above the rows:
	### the same fixed cells, 44 (the flag) + 120 + 80 + 120 + 116 (the marks)
	### = 480. Hover a heading for how its figure is counted.
	type gw_emitter_header = flowcontainer {
		direction = horizontal

		widget = {
			size = { 44 20 }
		}
		widget = {
			size = { 120 20 }

			textbox = {
				parentanchor = right|vcenter
				autoresize = yes
				max_width = 120
				elide = right
				align = right|nobaseline
				using = fontsize_small
				default_format = "#tooltippable"
				text = "gw_te_head_annual"
				tooltip = "gw_te_head_annual_tt"
			}
		}
		widget = {
			size = { 80 20 }

			textbox = {
				parentanchor = right|vcenter
				autoresize = yes
				max_width = 80
				elide = right
				align = right|nobaseline
				using = fontsize_small
				default_format = "#tooltippable"
				text = "gw_te_head_share"
				tooltip = "gw_te_head_share_tt"
			}
		}
		widget = {
			size = { 120 20 }

			textbox = {
				parentanchor = right|vcenter
				autoresize = yes
				max_width = 120
				elide = right
				align = right|nobaseline
				using = fontsize_small
				default_format = "#tooltippable"
				text = "gw_te_head_cum"
				tooltip = "gw_te_head_cum_tt"
			}
		}
		widget = {
			size = { 116 20 }
		}
	}

	### One market, named by its leader, on two lines, so a long name (up to
	### "United Socialist Council Republics of California", 48 characters)
	### has the whole 480 column. The second line is fixed cells under
	### gw_emitter_header's headings: the leader's flag (vanilla's tiny_flag:
	### its name on hover, the country on click), the annual figure, the share
	### of the world's, the cumulative total, and the marks: the treaty icon
	### while an Enforce Emissions Reduction treaty binds the leader, and "Our
	### market". The row's `visible` is on the outer widget and the leader's
	### capital, the datacontext, on the inner one, so an empty slot is never
	### read (the Space Race's Rivals rows and the UN's Security Council seats
	### do the same). Hover the row for the market's members and its cut.
	type gw_emitter_row = widget {
		size = { 480 50 }
		block "row_visible" {}

		flowcontainer = {
			direction = vertical
			spacing = 2
			block "row_context" {}
			tooltip = "gw_te_row_tt"

			textbox = {
				minimumsize = { 480 -1 }
				maximumsize = { 480 -1 }
				autoresize = yes
				elide = right
				align = left|nobaseline
				using = fontsize_medium
				default_format = "#tooltippable"
				text = "gw_te_row_name"
			}
			flowcontainer = {
				direction = horizontal

				widget = {
					size = { 44 24 }

					tiny_flag = {
						parentanchor = left|vcenter
						datacontext = "[State.GetCountry]"
					}
				}
				widget = {
					size = { 120 24 }

					textbox = {
						parentanchor = right|vcenter
						autoresize = yes
						max_width = 120
						elide = right
						align = right|nobaseline
						using = fontsize_medium
						default_format = "#v"
						text = "gw_te_row_annual"
					}
				}
				widget = {
					size = { 80 24 }

					textbox = {
						parentanchor = right|vcenter
						autoresize = yes
						max_width = 80
						elide = right
						align = right|nobaseline
						using = fontsize_medium
						default_format = "#v"
						text = "gw_te_row_share"
					}
				}
				widget = {
					size = { 120 24 }

					textbox = {
						parentanchor = right|vcenter
						autoresize = yes
						max_width = 120
						elide = right
						align = right|nobaseline
						using = fontsize_medium
						default_format = "#v"
						text = "gw_te_row_cum"
					}
				}
				widget = {
					size = { 116 24 }

					flowcontainer = {
						direction = horizontal
						parentanchor = right|vcenter
						spacing = 4
						ignoreinvisible = yes

						icon = {
							size = { 20 20 }
							parentanchor = vcenter
							visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( State.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('gw_disp_is_treaty_bound'), '(CFixedPoint)1' )]"
							texture = "gfx/interface/icons/diplomatic_treaties_articles_icons/enforce_emissions_reduction.dds"
							tooltip = "gw_te_treaty_tt"
						}
						textbox = {
							parentanchor = vcenter
							autoresize = yes
							max_width = 92
							elide = right
							align = right|nobaseline
							using = fontsize_small
							block "row_ours" {}
							text = "gw_te_ours"
						}
					}
				}
			}
		}
	}

	### Top Emitters: the five markets emitting most, largest first, each named
	### by its leader, with its annual and cumulative emissions and its share
	### of the world's; "+N more" lists the rest on hover; a line says where
	### our own market stands when it is not among the five. The rows come from
	### the viewer's snapshot (gw_top_emitters_refresh,
	### global_warming_effects.txt, monthly, players only); the figures on a
	### row are read live from the listed leader. A live list, so open by
	### default. Before the first January's figures, one line says when they
	### arrive, as the overview's table does; in the month at most between
	### the figures and the first snapshot, another says the list is coming
	### (gw_disp_emitters_state).
	type te_gw_sec_emitters = flowcontainer {
		direction = vertical
		parentanchor = hcenter
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		spacing = 4

		gw_section_header = {
			blockoverride "left_text" {
				text = "gw_sect_emitters"
			}
			blockoverride "onclick" {
				onclick = "[GetVariableSystem.Toggle('gw_emitters_closed')]"
			}
			blockoverride "onclick_showmore" {
				visible = "[GetVariableSystem.Exists('gw_emitters_closed')]"
			}
			blockoverride "onclick_showless" {
				visible = "[Not(GetVariableSystem.Exists('gw_emitters_closed'))]"
			}
		}

		gw_panel = {
			visible = "[Not(GetVariableSystem.Exists('gw_emitters_closed'))]"

			gw_text = {
				visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('gw_disp_emitters_state'), '(CFixedPoint)0' )]"
				align = hcenter|nobaseline
				text = "gw_emis_pending"
			}
			gw_text = {
				visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('gw_disp_emitters_state'), '(CFixedPoint)1' )]"
				align = hcenter|nobaseline
				text = "gw_te_list_pending"
			}

			flowcontainer = {
				direction = vertical
				ignoreinvisible = yes
				minimumsize = { 480 -1 }
				spacing = 4
				visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('gw_disp_emitters_state'), '(CFixedPoint)2' )]"

				gw_emitter_header = {
					visible = "[GreaterThanOrEqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('gw_disp_emitters_shown'), '(CFixedPoint)1' )]"
				}
				gw_emitter_row = {
					blockoverride "row_visible" {
						visible = "[GreaterThanOrEqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('gw_disp_emitters_shown'), '(CFixedPoint)1' )]"
					}
					blockoverride "row_context" {
						datacontext = "[JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.Var('gw_emitter_1').GetState]"
					}
					blockoverride "row_ours" {
						visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('gw_disp_emitters_own_slot'), '(CFixedPoint)1' )]"
					}
				}
				gw_emitter_row = {
					blockoverride "row_visible" {
						visible = "[GreaterThanOrEqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('gw_disp_emitters_shown'), '(CFixedPoint)2' )]"
					}
					blockoverride "row_context" {
						datacontext = "[JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.Var('gw_emitter_2').GetState]"
					}
					blockoverride "row_ours" {
						visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('gw_disp_emitters_own_slot'), '(CFixedPoint)2' )]"
					}
				}
				gw_emitter_row = {
					blockoverride "row_visible" {
						visible = "[GreaterThanOrEqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('gw_disp_emitters_shown'), '(CFixedPoint)3' )]"
					}
					blockoverride "row_context" {
						datacontext = "[JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.Var('gw_emitter_3').GetState]"
					}
					blockoverride "row_ours" {
						visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('gw_disp_emitters_own_slot'), '(CFixedPoint)3' )]"
					}
				}
				gw_emitter_row = {
					blockoverride "row_visible" {
						visible = "[GreaterThanOrEqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('gw_disp_emitters_shown'), '(CFixedPoint)4' )]"
					}
					blockoverride "row_context" {
						datacontext = "[JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.Var('gw_emitter_4').GetState]"
					}
					blockoverride "row_ours" {
						visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('gw_disp_emitters_own_slot'), '(CFixedPoint)4' )]"
					}
				}
				gw_emitter_row = {
					blockoverride "row_visible" {
						visible = "[GreaterThanOrEqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('gw_disp_emitters_shown'), '(CFixedPoint)5' )]"
					}
					blockoverride "row_context" {
						datacontext = "[JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.Var('gw_emitter_5').GetState]"
					}
					blockoverride "row_ours" {
						visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('gw_disp_emitters_own_slot'), '(CFixedPoint)5' )]"
					}
				}
				gw_text = {
					visible = "[GreaterThanOrEqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('gw_disp_emitters_total'), '(CFixedPoint)6' )]"
					align = hcenter|nobaseline
					text = "gw_te_more"
					tooltip = "[GetScriptedGui('gw_top_emitters_sgui').ExecuteTooltip( GuiScope.SetRoot( JournalEntry.GetCountry.GetCapital.MakeScope ).End )]"
				}
				# Our own market, when it is not among the five rows.
				gw_text = {
					visible = "[GreaterThanOrEqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('gw_disp_emitters_own_rank'), '(CFixedPoint)6' )]"
					align = hcenter|nobaseline
					text = "gw_te_own_rank"
				}
				gw_text = {
					visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.ScriptValue('gw_disp_emitters_own_rank'), '(CFixedPoint)0' )]"
					align = hcenter|nobaseline
					text = "gw_te_own_none"
				}
			}
		}
	}

	### History: two series from the shared history store, the global anomaly
	### (identical for everyone, stored per tracked country so it shares this
	### country's x-axis and the chart's country datamodel) and this market's
	### share of world emissions. Both are re-based each January, so both read
	### as staircases — see the legends. Open by default, as the UN's chart is.
	### Nothing here has an effect; the only click targets write GUI variables.
	type te_gw_sec_history = flowcontainer {
		direction = vertical
		parentanchor = hcenter
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		spacing = 4

		gw_section_header = {
			blockoverride "left_text" {
				text = "gw_sect_history"
			}
			blockoverride "onclick" {
				onclick = "[GetVariableSystem.Toggle('gw_hist_closed')]"
			}
			blockoverride "onclick_showmore" {
				visible = "[GetVariableSystem.Exists('gw_hist_closed')]"
			}
			blockoverride "onclick_showless" {
				visible = "[Not(GetVariableSystem.Exists('gw_hist_closed'))]"
			}
		}

		flowcontainer = {
			direction = vertical
			parentanchor = hcenter
			ignoreinvisible = yes
			spacing = 2
			visible = "[Not(GetVariableSystem.Exists('gw_hist_closed'))]"

			### Range selector — shared type, shared GUI variable, so switching the
			### range here also switches it on any other history chart in the game.
			flowcontainer = {
				direction = horizontal
				ignoreinvisible = yes
				parentanchor = hcenter
				spacing = 4
				margin = { 4 4 }

				te_history_range_button = {
					blockoverride "range_text" {
						text = "te_hist_range_1y"
					}
					blockoverride "range_enabled" {
						enabled = "[Not(GetVariableSystem.HasValue( 'te_hist_range', '1' ))]"
					}
					blockoverride "range_onclick" {
						onclick = "[GetVariableSystem.Set( 'te_hist_range', '1' )]"
					}
				}
				te_history_range_button = {
					blockoverride "range_text" {
						text = "te_hist_range_5y"
					}
					blockoverride "range_enabled" {
						enabled = "[Not(GetVariableSystem.HasValue( 'te_hist_range', '5' ))]"
					}
					blockoverride "range_onclick" {
						onclick = "[GetVariableSystem.Set( 'te_hist_range', '5' )]"
					}
				}
				te_history_range_button = {
					blockoverride "range_text" {
						text = "te_hist_range_20y"
					}
					blockoverride "range_enabled" {
						enabled = "[Or( GetVariableSystem.HasValue( 'te_hist_range', '1' ), GetVariableSystem.HasValue( 'te_hist_range', '5' ) )]"
					}
					blockoverride "range_onclick" {
						onclick = "[GetVariableSystem.Set( 'te_hist_range', '20' )]"
					}
				}
			}

			textbox = {
				visible = "[Not( IsDataModelEmpty( JournalEntry.GetCountry.MakeScope.GetList('te_hist') ) )]"
				parentanchor = hcenter
				autoresize = yes
				multiline = yes
				max_width = 480
				align = hcenter|nobaseline
				text = "te_hist_since"
			}

			### ---- Global temperature anomaly (0-4 C, the journal entry's scale) -
			te_history_chart = {
				blockoverride "chart_title" {
					text = "gw_hist_chart_temp_title"
				}
				blockoverride "chart_legend" {
					text = "gw_hist_chart_temp_legend"
				}
				# This series records no markers; the store's pips belong to
				# other systems (banking, cultural hegemony) and would go unexplained.
				blockoverride "marker_pips" {}
				blockoverride "bar_tooltip" {
					tooltip = "gw_hist_tt_temp"
				}
				blockoverride "bar_body" {
					te_history_bar_unsigned = {
						visible = "[ScriptContainer.HasVariable( 'te_hist_v_gw_temp' )]"
						blockoverride "values" {
							min = 0
							max = 4
							value = "[FixedPointToFloat( Max_CFixedPoint( '(CFixedPoint)0.08', ScriptContainer.GetVariableValue( 'te_hist_v_gw_temp' ) ) )]"
						}
						blockoverride "cover_values" {
							min = 0
							max = 4
							value = "[FixedPointToFloat( Max_CFixedPoint( '(CFixedPoint)0', Subtract_CFixedPoint( ScriptContainer.GetVariableValue( 'te_hist_v_gw_temp' ), '(CFixedPoint)0.16' ) ) )]"
						}
						blockoverride "color" {
							color = { 0.85 0.42 0.30 1.0 }
						}
					}
				}
			}

			### ---- This market's share of world emissions (0-100 %) -------------
			te_history_chart = {
				blockoverride "chart_title" {
					text = "gw_hist_chart_share_title"
				}
				blockoverride "chart_legend" {
					text = "gw_hist_chart_share_legend"
				}
				# This series records no markers; the store's pips belong to
				# other systems (banking, cultural hegemony) and would go unexplained.
				blockoverride "marker_pips" {}
				blockoverride "bar_tooltip" {
					tooltip = "gw_hist_tt_share"
				}
				blockoverride "bar_body" {
					te_history_bar_unsigned = {
						visible = "[ScriptContainer.HasVariable( 'te_hist_v_gw_share' )]"
						blockoverride "values" {
							min = 0
							max = 100
							value = "[FixedPointToFloat( Max_CFixedPoint( '(CFixedPoint)2', ScriptContainer.GetVariableValue( 'te_hist_v_gw_share' ) ) )]"
						}
						blockoverride "cover_values" {
							min = 0
							max = 100
							value = "[FixedPointToFloat( Max_CFixedPoint( '(CFixedPoint)0', Subtract_CFixedPoint( ScriptContainer.GetVariableValue( 'te_hist_v_gw_share' ), '(CFixedPoint)4' ) ) )]"
						}
						blockoverride "color" {
							color = { 0.45 0.60 0.40 1.0 }
						}
					}
				}
			}
		}
	}

	### "How Global Warming Works": every explanation, gathered into one
	### section at the foot, collapsed by default, one heading per topic (style
	### rule 1). The live sections above say what is happening; this says how
	### it works.
	type te_gw_sec_how = flowcontainer {
		direction = vertical
		parentanchor = hcenter
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		spacing = 4

		gw_section_header = {
			blockoverride "left_text" {
				text = "gw_how_header"
			}
			blockoverride "onclick" {
				onclick = "[GetVariableSystem.Toggle('gw_how_open')]"
			}
			blockoverride "onclick_showmore" {
				visible = "[Not(GetVariableSystem.Exists('gw_how_open'))]"
			}
			blockoverride "onclick_showless" {
				visible = "[GetVariableSystem.Exists('gw_how_open')]"
			}
		}

		gw_panel = {
			visible = "[GetVariableSystem.Exists('gw_how_open')]"

			gw_subheader = {
				blockoverride "subheader_margin" {}
				blockoverride "subheader_text" {
					text = "gw_how_sub_warming"
				}
			}
			gw_note = {
				text = "gw_how_warming_1"
			}
			gw_note = {
				text = "gw_how_warming_2"
			}
			gw_subheader = {
				blockoverride "subheader_text" {
					text = "gw_how_sub_penalty"
				}
			}
			gw_note = {
				text = "gw_how_penalty"
			}
			gw_subheader = {
				blockoverride "subheader_text" {
					text = "gw_how_sub_emissions"
				}
			}
			gw_note = {
				text = "gw_how_emissions_1"
			}
			gw_note = {
				text = "gw_how_emissions_2"
			}
			gw_subheader = {
				blockoverride "subheader_text" {
					text = "gw_how_sub_policies"
				}
			}
			gw_note = {
				text = "gw_how_policies_1"
			}
			gw_note = {
				text = "gw_how_policies_2"
			}
			gw_note = {
				text = "gw_how_policies_3"
			}
		}
	}

	### ======================================================================
	### COMPOSERS: the one order of the sections.
	### ======================================================================

	### Everything a returning player checks, open by default.
	type te_gw_status_sections = flowcontainer {
		direction = vertical
		parentanchor = hcenter
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		spacing = 4
		visible = "[JournalEntry.IsActive]"

		te_gw_sec_policies = {}
		te_gw_sec_emitters = {}
	}

	### The charts, then how it all works.
	type te_gw_reference_sections = flowcontainer {
		direction = vertical
		parentanchor = hcenter
		ignoreinvisible = yes
		spacing = 4
		visible = "[JournalEntry.IsActive]"

		te_gw_sec_history = {}
		te_gw_sec_how = {}
	}
}

### ==========================================================================
### JOURNAL ENTRY ROOTS (je_global_warming.txt). Bare wrappers that repeat the
### composers' IsActive gate, so an inactive entry's containers collapse.
###
### je_global_warming has is_shown_when_inactive and stays inactive until the
### world has warmed by 0.1 C, which is decades on a normal game. Until then
### the entry renders greyed for every country and none of this content means
### anything, so nothing is drawn at all — which also stops the per-frame
### ExecuteTooltip work for countries that will never look at the panel
### (gui_modding_guide.md gotcha #14).
### ==========================================================================
flowcontainer = {
	name = "widget_je_gw_overview"
	visible = "[JournalEntry.IsActive]"
	parentanchor = hcenter
	ignoreinvisible = yes

	te_gw_overview_panel = {}
}

flowcontainer = {
	name = "widget_je_gw_status"
	visible = "[JournalEntry.IsActive]"
	parentanchor = hcenter
	ignoreinvisible = yes

	te_gw_status_sections = {}
}

flowcontainer = {
	name = "widget_je_gw_reference"
	visible = "[JournalEntry.IsActive]"
	parentanchor = hcenter
	ignoreinvisible = yes

	te_gw_reference_sections = {}
}
